It seems that this recursion logic is to do
- visit all sensors via recursion
- invoke callback at the last sensor (or at the end of visits)

However, I think this may require too much deeper stack consumption.
So, this can be flattened by doing
- go visit each sensor by a simple loop
- and invoke the callback at the last sensor visit
- The last visit can be checked by using a shared_ptr of 'visit-count'


```
inline void getSensorsByPurpose(
    const std::shared_ptr<bmcweb::AsyncResp>& asyncResp,
    const SensorServicePathList& sensorListIn,
    ...callback)
{

    // Count of asyncCall invocations. If it reaches to 0, all of them are
    // executed
    std::shared_ptr<int> remainingSensorsToVist =
        std::make_shared<int>(sensorListIn.size());

    for (const SensorServicePathMap& nextSensor : sensorListIn)
    {
       ...
        dbus::utility::getProperty<std::vector<std::string>>(...,
            [asyncResp, ..., nextSensor, remainingSensorsToVist](
                ...  purposeList) {

                (*remainingSensorsToVist)--; // visited

                if (ec ... )
                {
                    ...
                    if ((*remainingSensorsToVist) == 0)
                    {
                        callback(ec, sensorMatches);
                    }
                    return;
                }

                if (!ec)
                {
                    checkSensorPurpose(nextSensor, sensorPurpose, sensorMatches,
                                       purposeList);
                }

                if ((*remainingSensorsToVist) == 0)
                {
                    callback(ec, sensorMatches);
                }
            });
```

If the error may need to be collected, the errors can be kept as a shared_ptr (along with remainingSensorsToVisit).
